  "attribution_note": "Classical regular polygon face-contact lattices with complete guillotine composition. PingYou Ltd supplies the finite translational seam returns and complete native certificates; the source lattices are not claimed as new.",
  "construction": {
   "name": "whole_staggered_column_seam_return",
   "proof": "Forced face-contact staggered columns for octagonal and dodecagonal prisms\n\nOctagon: put a=(1+sqrt(2))/2 and b=1/2. The ideal flat-oriented regular octagon has vertices(+-a,+-b),(+-b,+-a), with |x|,|y|<=a and |x+y|,|x-y|<=a+b. Define the column step h=(3+sqrt(2))/2 and full vertical period v=2a=1+sqrt(2). The owner centers are(h*i,v*j+a*(i mod2)). Owners in one column separate by the horizontal face normal. In neighboring columns their minimal vertical offset is a, and h+a=2(a+b), so a diagonal face normal separates them. Columns two or more apart separate on x since2h>2a. Thus these whole octagons form the classical dense staggered lattice. This is the standard face-contact lattice seen after its forced45-degree symmetry change, not a tuned angle.\n\nDodecagon: put a=(2+sqrt(3))/2, v=2a and h=sqrt(3)*a=(3+2sqrt(3))/2. The ideal flat-oriented regular dodecagon has apothem a and support normals at integer multiples of30degrees. Use centers(h*i,v*j+a*(i mod2)). One-column pairs separate on y. Neighboring columns at the minimal offset a separate along the30-degree face normal because (sqrt(3)/2)*h+a/2=2a. More distant columns separate on x because2h>2a. These are complete dodecagons in the standard triangular face-contact lattice. The column direction is forced by those face contacts.\n\nFor either source, a c-column by r-row patch consists of every whole owner with0<=i<c,0<=j<r. Its exact bounding box dimensions are(v+(c-1)*h,v*r+epsilon*v/2,L), epsilon=1 if c>1 and0 otherwise. Its midpoint is((c-1)*h/2,(r-1)*v/2+epsilon*v/4,0). Both side costs and the unmatched staggered end are retained. The ideal owner frame is fixed at pi/8 for the octagon or pi/12 for the dodecagon relative to the canonical source. No angle is searched.\n\nApply the complete heterogeneous row/layer rule: for a fixed layer thickness, a row contains floor(S/module_width) identical whole patches; rows of possibly different patch types concatenate with their full row heights. Layers concatenate with their full thicknesses. Keep each proper axis-permutation quaternion and act on the whole patch, including every owner frame. The full backpointer word is an inverse decoder. Distinct boxes have disjoint interiors, and every within-patch pair has the source separator just proved. A named suffix of whole owners may be deleted while retaining its complete parent.\n\nAll costs lie in(p+q*sqrt(d))/2 with nonnegative integers p,q, d=2 or3. The finite cost dynamic program retains an actual row/layer word and does not solve a free angle. Binary64 quaternions in native files are a nearby numerical realization with a common outward margin; native certification checks their exact represented rotations, every owner vertex and every pair separately. The ideal source theorem does not silently replace that native check.\n\nSliding the physical seam of a complete staggered polygon patch\n\nKeep the ideal owner frames and the full vertical period v=2a of STAGGERED_POLYGON_GUILLOTINE_PROOF.txt. Let neighboring columns alternate between offsets0 anddelta, with1<=delta<=a. Their minimum vertical displacement modulo v isdelta, since delta<=v/2. Preserve one actual separating face contact by defining the horizontal column step\n  octagon: h(delta)=2(a+1/2)-delta;\n  dodecagon: h(delta)=(4a-delta)/sqrt(3).\nFor the octagon, h+delta=2(a+1/2) is its diagonal face support equality. For the dodecagon,(sqrt(3)/2)h+delta/2=2a is its30-degree face equality. At delta=a these are the retained densest staggered source steps. At delta=1, h=2a in both cases. Within1<=delta<=a, h>=the densest step>a, so columns two or more apart separate on x; owners in one column separate on y by v. Every intermediate source is therefore a complete physical packing. Delta is a translational return parameter, not an owner-frame angle.\n\nA c by r whole patch has exact box dimensions\n  W(delta)=v+(c-1)h(delta), H(delta)=r*v+epsilon*delta, Z=L,\nwith epsilon=1 ifc>1 and0 otherwise. Its midpoint is((c-1)h/2,(r-1)v/2+epsilon*delta/2,0). Thus sliding the seam transfers width to one actual boundary end cost, while retaining all c*r whole owners and their marked face contacts.\n\nFix a complete guillotine assembly word from the earlier control bank. Allow one delta per row of congruent modules. For each row impose module_count*its actual x width<=S. For each layer impose the sum of actual row heights<=S and a common layer thickness at least every row module's z thickness. Finally impose the sum of full layer thicknesses<=S. These are linear inequalities in the row deltas, layer thicknesses and common host sideS. Solving that linear closure system realizes the fixed physical return word; it does not search angles, change the number of owners or forget box end costs.\n\nThe inverse decoder places the full chosen layers and rows on their consecutive actual intervals, centers each row's modules, then rebuilds every shifted source-column owner. All parent/deletion words and the original unslid control are retained. Native certification checks the actual serialized quaternion rotations, every owner vertex and every pair; the floating LP alone is not a proof certificate.\n",
